# Fixture for the quick-fix path, with an EXPLICITLY DECLARED local.
#
# Vector is a real class in gen_collect.obl but is not in scope without a 'use',
# so analysis reports "Undefined class or enum" -- the diagnostic
# Document.CodeAction offers a fix for.
#
# The declaration is deliberately `v : Vector;` and not `v := Vector->New()`:
# the two reach the fix by different routes, and both are now covered.
#
# This one matches a symbol-table entry whose TYPE is the class, which also
# supplies the position of `Vector` inside the type. Its diagnostic is anchored
# on the VARIABLE (`v`), not on the class, which is why that position has to
# come from the entry. The sibling lsp_codeaction.obs takes the other route: no
# entry exists for an inferred local, but its diagnostic IS anchored on the
# class token, so the diagnostic's own range is the insertion point (#1057).
#
# Until #1055 the `:=` fixture was the only test of this path and it could not
# reach it, so the applied edits had no coverage at all -- which is how #1052
# shipped a fix naming the wrong bundle for twenty-two class names.
class NeedsUseDeclared {
	function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
		v : Vector;
		v->Size()->PrintLine();
	}
}
